---
alwaysApply: true
---
Use TypeScript for all backend code.

Structure API with MVC or feature-based architecture (routes/, controllers/, services/, middleware/, types/).

Use express-async-handler or similar to handle async errors.

Validate input with zod or Joi, especially on API endpoints.

Use environment variables (dotenv) for config (e.g., DB_URL, PORT).

Keep routes RESTful and modularized (/api/v1/users, /api/v1/auth, etc.).

Centralize error handling using a global error middleware.

Protect routes using middleware (e.g., auth check, role-based access control).

Use logging (e.g., morgan, winston) for debugging and monitoring in dev/prod.

Use helmet, cors, rate-limit, and other security middleware in production.

Write unit and integration tests using Jest or Vitest + supertest.